Here’s a simple and efficient JavaScript function that removes duplicate values from an array:

```js
/**
 * Removes duplicate values from an array.
 *
 * @param {Array} arr - The input array.
 * @returns {Array} A new array with duplicates removed.
 */
function removeDuplicates(arr) {
  if (!Array.isArray(arr)) {
    throw new TypeError('Input must be an array');
  }

  const seen = new Set();
  const result = [];

  for (const item of arr) {
    if (seen.has(item)) {
      continue;
    }
    seen.add(item);
    result.push(item);
  }

  return result;
}

// Example usage:
const input = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5];
console.log(removeDuplicates(input)); // [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
```

This uses a `Set` to track seen elements and builds a new array with only unique values. It preserves the order of first occurrence.
